WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:00.740
You know,

1
00:00:00.939 --> 00:00:04.078
I've been really struggling with my roommate's loud music lately.

2
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:06.909
That sounds really frustrating.

3
00:00:07.329 --> 00:00:09.810
It's tough to study with distractions like that.

4
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.350
Exactly

5
00:00:12.159 --> 00:00:15.319
I just don't know how to bring it up without making things awkward.

6
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.459
One approach you might consider is using an I statement when you talk to her.

7
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.219
An I statement.

8
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:23.969
What does that mean?

9
00:00:24.889 --> 00:00:28.629
It's a way to express how you feel without sounding accusatory.

10
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.040
Instead of saying,

11
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.090
you're always playing loud music,

12
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:32.869
you could say,

13
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.680
I feel frustrated when the music is loud because

14
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.389
it makes it hard for me to concentrate.

15
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:38.830
Oh,

16
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:39.590
I see.

17
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.389
So it focuses on my feelings rather than blaming her.

18
00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.540
Exactly.

19
00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:50.409
It helps the other person understand your perspective without getting defensive.

20
00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:53.189
It's a more constructive way to communicate.

21
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.479
That makes so much sense.

22
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.770
I can see how it would lead to a better conversation.

23
00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:00.930
Definitely.

24
00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:04.709
Effective communication is key in any relationship,

25
00:01:05.069 --> 00:01:06.699
especially when living together.

26
00:01:07.089 --> 00:01:08.389
Thanks for explaining that.

27
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.970
I think I'll try it out next time.